     26          /* General Notes: Define one device to compile options for that device. */
     27          /* Will not compile correctly if no device is defined.  Not all options */
     28          /* for each device are supported.  There is no error checking for data  */
     29          /* entry.  Defines may not remove all code that is not relevant to the  */
     30          /* device. This example was written for an 8051-type micro, the DS2250/ */
     31          /* DS5000.  The program must be modified to work properly on typical    */
     32          /* 8051 variants (i.e. assign I2C bus to unused port pins).  This       */
     33          /* program is for example only and is not supported by Dallas Maxim     */
